#import "@preview/abntly:0.1.1": *

= Introduction

This document is an example of an academic work typeset with the abntly package. It has two aims: to show the
result of each element of the structure defined by @nbr 14724:2024, and to be the starting point of a new work. The
code of the example is divided into a main file, with the pre-textual and the post-textual elements, and a file for
each chapter.

The standard organizes the work in three parts. The pre-textual elements go from the title page to the summary. The
textual elements are the introduction, the development and the conclusion. The post-textual elements are the
references, the glossary, the appendices, the annexes and the index @abnt2024.

== Aims

The general aim of this example is to gather, in one document, every element of an academic work. The specific aims
are:
+ to show the pre-textual and the post-textual elements, in the order defined by the standard;
+ to show how each element of the text is written, in @ch-elements[Chapter];
+ to offer filler text for the other chapters, so that the pagination, the running header and the summary can be
  seen in a document of several pages.

== Organization of the document

@ch-elements[Chapter] presents the elements of the text. @ch-background[Chapter] and @ch-results[Chapter] hold
filler text, a table that takes more than one page and a table lying on its side. @ch-conclusion[Chapter] closes
the text.
